+## Firebase apps
+
+An app that keeps Firebase Auth underneath (security rules, App Check) signs in here, then swaps its
+access token for a Firebase custom token and calls `signInWithCustomToken`. The Firebase uid is the accounts `sub`.
+
+```
+POST /t/{tenant}/v1/firebase/{projectId}/token   Authorization: Bearer <access token>
+→ { token, uid, email, expires_in: 3600 }
+```
+
+Enable a project for a tenant by storing its service-account JSON (Firebase console → Project settings →
+Service accounts → Generate new private key):
+
+```
+aws ssm put-parameter --name /accounts/firebase/<tenant>/<projectId> --type SecureString --value file://key.json
+```
+
+No parameter means 404. Mobile apps register their own redirect scheme (`com.example.app:/oauth2redirect`);
+such clients are served as OIDC `native` clients.
+
 - **Design:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-accounts-platform-design.md`
 - **P1 plan:** `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-19-accounts-p1.md`
